}}

==Enemy==
Bun Bun Black is a bigger and bulkier variant of [[Teacher Bun Bun]]. However, his speed and damage pales in comparison to the original Bun Bun. Combined with his dual-trait weakness, Bun Bun Black is actually easier to handle in most cases.

==Strategy==
Bun Bun Black has a lot of health, but surprisingly low pushing power. In most of his appearances, he has over 1.4 million health, but his dual-trait weakness can help bring that down very rapidly. Use [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to burst him down, as he generally acts as a wall for dangerous backliners like [[Sunfish Jones]], [[Director Kurosawah]] and [[Golem Sunfish]]. In such cases, you actually want to keep him alive so that your main DPS units don't walk into their range too early. Treat him like a wall, but for both sides; he blocks your units from pushing, but he also blocks enemy backliners from attacking your DPS units.

